It is Monday afternoon, and I am off from work.
I take the bus from the software company.
But I do not go directly home.
I get off the bus at the large pedestrian street.
I walk over to the clothing store from Saturday.
In my bag, I have the blue cotton shirt.
It is still completely new and unworn.
The shirt is too small, so I would like to try a bigger one.
I hope that they have it in another size.
I walk into the bright store.
I walk directly up to the cash register.
I open my wallet and find my receipt.
I hold it ready in my hand.
Then I take the shirt out of my bag.
A friendly clerk stands behind the counter.
She looks up and smiles at me.
I smile back.
I stand ready with the shirt and the receipt in my hands.
